      <file>.claude/skills/adr-check/SKILL.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">This task runs MAIN-SESSION, not delegated to a sub-agent — `.claude/adr/ADR-047-notification-action-spine.md`, `.claude/adr/INDEX.md`, and `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` are all `.claude/`-adjacent or project-tracking writes the sub-agent write boundary (root CLAUDE.md §3) forbids for parallel agents.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-clause-7">`/test-diet` MUST run BEFORE the project is marked complete (root CLAUDE.md §7 project-close test diet gate). It is read-only — it emits `git rm`/`git mv` commands; a human/this task's operator executes them, this task does not silently auto-delete tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-clause-6.5">Any code-review/adr-check finding that reflects a deliberate, already-surfaced ADR Tension (e.g. the ADR-043 Notification-flip tension logged in spec.md's ADR Tensions table, Path C) is NOT re-litigated here as a new violation — cite the existing resolution. A genuinely NEW finding follows the three-path protocol (A/B/C) with the required output format; it is not silently waived.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every one of the 11 numbered items in spec.md's "Success Criteria" section and every checkbox in README.md's "Graduation Criteria" section MUST be individually verified with a concrete pointer (test name, file, or note) — a criterion is not checked off on the basis that "the phase ran," it is checked off against its own Verify clause.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">ADR-047 full finalization MUST reflect the FR-01 mode decision (task 001's spike outcome) verbatim — do not restate a generic "SignalR" placement without citing the decided mode (Serverless/Default) and its rationale.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/test-diet/SKILL.md</file>
