    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="ADR full-version finalization" location="docs/adr/">Follow the shape of an already-Accepted full ADR (e.g. docs/adr/ADR-048-communication-participant-index.md) for section structure; the concise `.claude/adr/ADR-047-*.md` from task 010 is the source-of-truth decision content to expand, not a separate draft.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Data-model entity doc" location="docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md">Follow this file's shape (schema table, relationships, JSON field notes) for the outbox table's finalized entry.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Confirm every dependency task (001,010,011,012,013,020,021,022,023,024,025,030,031,032,033,040,041,042,050,051,052) shows ✅ in `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`; if any is not ✅, STOP and escalate rather than proceeding (this task is the terminal gate, not a task-completer).</step>
    <step order="2">Run `/code-review` against the full set of project-touched files (Phases 0-5 combined diff vs the project's base commit).</step>
    <step order="3">Run `/adr-check` against the same diff.</step>
    <step order="4">Triage every finding from steps 2-3: fix (Path C), cite an already-documented exception/tension (Path A, spec.md ADR Tensions), or escalate a new amendment candidate (Path B) per root CLAUDE.md §6.5 — do not leave any finding unresolved and undocumented.</step>
    <step order="5">Run `/test-diet` (ADR-038 §7 build-vs-maintain classifier) against every test added/modified across the project's tasks; write `notes/test-diet-report.md`; execute the reviewer-approved `git rm`/`git mv` commands it emits.</step>
    <step order="6">Finalize `docs/adr/ADR-047-notification-action-spine.md` (full version): expand the concise `.claude/adr/ADR-047-notification-action-spine.md` (task 010) into the full ADR shape, explicitly reflecting the FR-01 mode decision, the Phase 3 ADR-043 Notification-flip resolution (Path C), and any deviations logged in `projects/spaarke-notification-spine-r1/notes/` across Phases 1-5.</step>
    <step order="7">Update `.claude/adr/INDEX.md`'s ADR-047 row to `Accepted` (or the correct terminal status) and append a `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` entry for the ADR-047 finalization.</step>
    <step order="8">Finalize the outbox table's `docs/data-model/` entry (task 011's actual table/column names) — schema table, relationships (ADR-024 regarding lookup), JSON envelope column shape, delivered/dismissed/expiry semantics.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `/repo-cleanup` for the project.</step>
    <step order="10">Walk every checkbox in `README.md`'s "Graduation Criteria" section and every numbered item in `spec.md`'s "Success Criteria" section; check each off with a concrete verification pointer (test name / file path / note reference); do not check off any item without a pointer.</step>
    <step order="11">Update `README.md` status to `Complete` (top status line + Current Status table); update `plan.md` status to `Complete`.</step>
    <step order="12">Write `notes/lessons-learned.md`: what worked (wave ordering unblocking messaging-r3 early, the gate-zero spike), what was harder than expected, any ADR-047 deviations from the original design, and open items handed to sibling projects (messaging-r3, spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r1, spaarke-daily-update-service-r5).</step>
    <step order="13">Verify `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` shows ✅ for all 21 prior tasks plus this one.</step>
    <step order="14">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to ✅ completed</step>
    <step order="15">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-notification-spine-r1/notes/</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any dependency task is not ✅ complete when this task starts, STOP and escalate — do not attempt wrap-up against an incomplete project.</trigger>
    <trigger>If /code-review or /adr-check surfaces a Critical finding with no existing ADR Tension covering it, STOP and run the root CLAUDE.md §6.5 protocol before proceeding to closure.</trigger>
  </escalation>

